    "margin": "low",
    "rationale": "The biopsy of the intact papule shows the defining features of leukocytoclastic vasculitis: perivascular neutrophilic infiltrate, vessel wall necrosis, and fibrinoid necrosis, with clinical ulcers and eschars. R4 is the most specific supported label; R5 is the same process but less specific. Wegener's lacks granulomatous/respiratory/renal features, lupus is weakly supported by ANA/SSA but contradicted by high MPO and normal complement, and PAN/erythema induratum lack supporting histology.",
